  [1mHow the filters combine.[0m The quick filters and the Event type Select both filter by type, so choosing one resets the
  other to "All events". The date range is applied on top. Changing a preset fills in the date fields, and editing a
  date switches the preset to Custom. Dates are compared in the viewer's time zone, the same zone the table shows. If To
  is before From, the fields show "The end date must be after the start date." (linked with [38;5;153maria-describedby[39m) and the
  previous results stay. A single-day range is allowed. Filtering happens on change, and pressing Enter does nothing.

  [1mNo-JS.[0m The filter markup is in the HTML with the [38;5;153mhidden[39m attribute, and the script reveals it. The rows themselves are
  already rendered by JS, which breaks the NOTES.md rule. That gap predates this work, and I'm leaving it out of scope
  unless you want it fixed.

  [1mFiles and commits:[0m
  1. [38;5;153mstyle:[39m adds [38;5;153mpublic/tokens.css[39m with only the tokens this page uses, links it from [38;5;153mactivity.html[39m, and converts
     [38;5;153mactivity.css[39m to use it (no raw hex, px or durations). About 100 lines.
  2. [38;5;153mfeat:[39m adds the filter markup to [38;5;153mactivity.html[39m, the filter logic to [38;5;153mactivity.js[39m, and the filter styles to
     [38;5;153mactivity.css[39m. The bar follows the 01–04 specs: labels above the controls, a 2px focus ring, 24px minimum targets, a
     fieldset for the radio group, and wrapping down to 320px. About 200 lines.

  I'll show you the full diff before each commit and won't push anything.

